{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1764,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The Shah keeps adding drummers, and every drum makes his feast more boring.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 130
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "shah",
   "text": "Louder! This music must never stop!",
   "from": 134,
   "to": 220
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It's his victory feast. The first song sent his joy needle to the top.",
   "from": 224,
   "to": 314
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Out in the yard, a blacksmith hammers a plain iron ring.",
   "from": 318,
   "to": 389
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But hours later, the same music barely moves the needle.",
   "from": 392,
   "to": 484
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So he orders more musicians, then a bigger drum, then one the size of a cart.",
   "from": 487,
   "to": 610
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It rolls off the stage and flattens the flute player.",
   "from": 614,
   "to": 668
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The blacksmith offers his ring. It reads: this too shall pass.",
   "from": 671,
   "to": 781
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "shah",
   "text": "Nothing passes! Not my party!",
   "from": 785,
   "to": 874
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He hurls the ring. It snaps a lute string, and the whole hall goes silent.",
   "from": 878,
   "to": 982
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then the music starts again, and the needle shoots past the top.",
   "from": 985,
   "to": 1049
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, in two thousand nine, researchers tested TV shows with and without ad breaks.",
   "from": 1065,
   "to": 1198
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "People said they'd rather skip the breaks. But breaks made the shows more fun.",
   "from": 1201,
   "to": 1289
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Joy fades as you get used to it, a spring dragging the needle down.",
   "from": 1293,
   "to": 1386
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A break cuts the spring, and the needle jumps back up.",
   "from": 1389,
   "to": 1490
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "It fails for people who barely get used to anything.",
   "from": 1494,
   "to": 1555
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So now the Shah stops his own band every hour, with a gong.",
   "from": 1559,
   "to": 1641
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And your favorite show? It just cut to an ad.",
   "from": 1645,
   "to": 1740
  }
 ],
